# Prismic slices

## Settings

Every slice has a `settings` group: `padding_top`, `padding_bottom`, `theme`.
Pass them to the Lumos `Section` that wraps the slice.

Theme default is always `inherit` in the model and in code:

```tsx
theme={slice.primary.settings?.theme ?? "inherit"}
```

Never default a new slice to `dark`, `light`, or `brand`.

## CSS

No CSS strings or `Styles` helper in slice JSX. Put styles in
`src/slices/<Name>/index.css` under `@layer components`, and import that file
from `index.tsx`.

## Screenshots

After building or changing a slice visually, save `screenshot-default.png` in
that slice folder (about one viewport of the section).

## Content

Fill the section’s Prismic content (copy, links, images, settings) in the same
pass as the model and component. Publish after writing. See
`.agents/skills/lumos-prismic/SKILL.md`.
